{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>A roaring lion, a ruler</b> — [verses 15–16] the kaf is lacking." "<b>That prowls</b> — from the root שוק, meaning tramples. So a ruler who is wicked over a poor people, and likewise a ruler who lacks understanding, is likened to a lion and to a bear in his oppression of the poor."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:25:13.969996411Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}